#: {{ant|en|unfortunate|unlucky}}
#* {{quote-book|en|1661|w:Robert Boyle|chapter=The Conclusion|w:The Sceptical Chymist|location=w:London|publisher=J. Cadwell||429|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=pxhKAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA429|oclc=4477054|passage={{...}} I think I may presume that what I have hitherto Diſcourſed will induce you to think, that Chymists have been much more '''happy''' in finding Experiments than the Cauſes of them; or in aſſigning the Principles by which they may beſt be explain’d.}}
#* {{RQ:Austen Northanger Abbey|I|XIV|256|"Historians, you think," said Miss Tilney, "are not '''happy''' in their flights of fancy. They display imagination without raising interest. {{nb...}}"}}
