##* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XLIII|66|How fares it with the '''happy''' dead?}}
# [[content#Adjective|Content]], [[willing]], [[satisfied]] (with or to do something); having no [[objection]] (to something).
#: {{syn|en|pleased}}
#: {{ant|en|disenchanted|dissatisfied}}
#: {{ux|en|Are you '''happy''' to pay me back by the end of the week?}}
#: {{ux|en|Yes, I am '''happy''' with the decision.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|1844||Patience and Perseverance|editor=w:[[Joseph Barker (minister)|Joseph Barker]]|The Christian|location=w:London|publisher=w:[[Chapman & Hall|Chapman]]||volume=1|issue=14|314|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=J4AXAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA314|oclc=8266193|A Christian may be '''happier''' in low circumstances, than in high ones. He may be '''happier''' without rich friends, than with them. He may be '''happier''' in loneliness, than in a crowd of flatterers. He may be '''happier''' under reproach, than when riding on the spring-tide of popularity. He may be '''happier''' with hard work, than in a life of ease. He may be '''happier''' with coarse and scanty food, than with tables of luxury. He may be '''happier''' in sickness and persecution, than in health and quietness.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|2007|Iver David Reingold|chapter=Substitution Reactions|Organic Chemistry, or, “The Happy Carbon”: An Introduction Emphasizing Biological Connections|location=w:Delhi|publisher=Indo American Books||308|isbn=9788189617394|A strong acid is also a substance whose conjugate base (obviously a weak base) is quite '''happy''' with the excess electrons it got from that bond.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|2016|Imad A. Moosa|chapter=The Post-crisis Regulatory Landscape: An Overview|Contemporary Issues in the Post-crisis Regulatory Landscape|location=w:Singapore|publisher=w:World Scientific||8|isbn=9789813109285|This wave of "financial innovation" led to rapid growth in subprime lending, which was enhanced on the demand side by the housing boom and general asset price bubble. While the party lasted everyone was '''happy'''. Mortgage lenders were '''happy''' to lend and keep subprime loans off their books via securitization. Issuers of ABSs were '''happy''' to get their commissions. Borrowers were '''happy''' to get loans without scrutiny. Investors were '''happy''' to acquire assets that were "risk-free" and offered a return of hundreds of basis points over that offered by US Treasuries.}}
# {{lb|en|of acts, events, speech, etc.}} {{cap|bringing}} or [[being]] an instance of [[favourable]] [[fortune]]; [[apt]], [[felicitous]], [[fortunate]], [[propitious]].
#: {{ant|en|inapt|unfelicitous|unfortunate|unpropitious}}
#: {{co|en|'''happy''' coincidence}}
#* {{quote-book|en|1792|James Thomson|chapter=Letter XXXI. From the Hon. Miss Wilton to Mr. Benfield.|The Denial; or, The Happy Retreat|edition=2nd corr.|location=w:London|volume=1||185|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=E0BWAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA185|oclc=642654779|The common privilege of your ſex affords you the '''happy''' opportunity of alleviating your ſorrows by communicating your ſentiments and feelings to some faithful friend; but to women, even this relief is rigidly denied, and, bound by the harſh reſtraints which the delicacy and reſerve of female natures have impoſed, I muſt bear the ſecret of my ſorrows with painful ſilence.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|1804|[James Stephen]|The Opportunity; or, Reasons for an Immediate Alliance with St. Domingo|location=w:London|publisher=w:Charles Whittingham||101|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=hMFeAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA101|oclc=65238401|You would, even by this most favourable result, be at best only replaced in the situation, and restored to the '''happy''' opportunity which you at present possess:{{…}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Jean Baudrillard|tlr=Chris Turner|title=Cool Memories|location=London; New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:Verso Books|year=1990|page=138|isbn=978-0-86091-500-3|passage=When happy events coincide, that is a '''happy''' coincidence. But the coincidence of baneful events is a '''happy''' coincidence too.}}
#* {{RQ:Fry Liar|41|‘I had the '''happy''' notion of adding an egg,’ Williams shouted back. ‘It [[poach]]es in the soup. Not unlike an Italian ''[[stracciatella]]''. Singularly toothsome.{{nb...}}’}}
#* {{quote-journal|en||date=2022-12-15|Samanth Subramanian|Dismantling Sellafield: the epic task of shutting down a nuclear site|The Guardian|https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/dec/15/dismantling-sellafield-epic-task-shutting-down-decomissioned-nuclear-site||The UK’s earliest reactors – a type called Magnox – were set up to harvest plutonium for bombs; the electricity was a '''happy''' byproduct.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261013075133/https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2022/dec/15/dismantling-sellafield-epic-task-shutting-down-decomissioned-nuclear-site|archivedate=13 October 2026}}
# {{lb|en|in combination}} [[favoring|Favoring]] or [[inclined]] to use.
#: {{ux|en|[[slap'''happy''']], [[trigger-'''happy''']]}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Dan Benson|chapter=Stupid Mistake #9: Following Fads vs. Staying the Course|title=12 Stupid Mistakes People Make with Their Money|location=Nashville, Tenn.|publisher=[[w:Thomas Nelson (publisher)|Thomas Nelson]]|year=2002|page=128|isbn=978-0-8499-1681-6|passage=We live in a sue-'''happy''' society. If Santa slides off your roof and busts his tailbone, he could sue you, and probably will.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Jason Heller|title=[[w:The Darkness (band)|The Darkness]]: ''Hot Cakes'' [music review]|url=http://www.avclub.com/articles/the-darkness-hot-cakes,84036/|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120824002343/http://www.avclub.com/articles/the-darkness-hot-cakes%2C84036/|archivedate=24 August 2012|work=w:The A.V. Club|date=21 August 2012|passage=“Baby, I was a loser / Several years on the dole / An Englishman with a very high voice / Doing rock ’n’ roll,” sings falsetto-'''happy''' frontman {{w|Justin Hawkins}} at the start of “Every Inch Of You,” ''{{w|Hot Cakes}}''’ opener.}}
# {{lb|en|rare|of people|often followed by "at" or "in"}} [[dexterous|Dexterous]], [[ready]], [[skilful]].
#* {{quote-book|en|1761|Simon Wagstaff [pseudonym; {{w|Jonathan Swift}}]|w:A Complete Collection of Genteel and Ingenious Conversation|location=w:Edinburgh|section=introduction|https://www.google.com/books/edition/i/3lMJAAAAQAAJ|iii|For inſtance, one lady can give an anſwer better than aſk a queſtion: one gentleman is '''happy''' at a reply; another excels in a rejoinder: one can revive a languiſhing converſation by a ſudden ſurpriſing ſentence; another is more dextrous in ſeconding; a third can fill the gap with laughing, or commending what has been ſaid.}}
